{"created": "2026-09-07T07:22:46.633127+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-07T07:22:46.893469+00:00", "id": 22637968, "conceptrecid": "22637967", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22637968", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22637967", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22637968", "metadata": {"title": "Single Peaks in Truncated Stieltjes Integral Equations", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22637968", "publication_date": "2026-09-07", "description": "<p>We study maxima of curves defined by normalized, truncated Stieltjes integrals. For a positive profile h, strict decrease of its elasticity xh'(x)/h(x) on its declining side gives a unique nondegenerate maximum at every level for which the curve exists. This proves a uniqueness conjecture of Viakhirev and makes its additional existence hypotheses unnecessary. We treat every positive power of the kernel, on a finite interval or the positive half-line: all positive levels occur for powers at least one, whereas a uniquely maximized boundary integral gives the exact level threshold for smaller powers. We determine the movement and limiting positions of the peak. For log-normal densities, the normalized polynomial cutoffs proposed by Viakhirev have maximizing locations and heights converging at rate O(R^-1) to limits independent of the cutoff exponent. In contrast, smooth strictly unimodal profiles can produce arbitrarily many critical points.</p><p>This version presents complete mathematical proofs. These proofs have not yet been formalized in a proof assistant. Formal verification is planned; under the author's verification standard, this version is archived as a dated preprint, with active promotion of its results deferred until formal verification is complete.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Li, Alex Chengyu", "affiliation": "Independent Researcher, Tokyo, Japan", "orcid": "0009-0008-4516-8946"}], "keywords": ["Stieltjes integral", "implicit integral equation", "unimodality", "log-concavity", "log-normal distribution", "critical points"], "version": "1.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22637967"}}]}}, "title": "Single Peaks in Truncated Stieltjes Integral Equations", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22637968", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22637968", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22637968?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22637968", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22637968", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22637968", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22637968/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22637967", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22637967", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22637967", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22637967", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22637968/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22637968/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22637968/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22637968/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22637968:truncated-stieltjes-peaks-v1.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22637968:truncated-stieltjes-peaks-v1.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22637968:truncated-stieltjes-peaks-v1.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22637968:truncated-stieltjes-peaks-v1.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22637968:truncated-stieltjes-peaks-v1.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22637968:truncated-stieltjes-peaks-v1.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "h